      },
      "lineNbr": 152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000353
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T08:49:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For this specific case — a compile-time prefix literal concatenated with a single const char* value — operator+ is equivalent or marginally faster. std::format is genuinely beneficial when formatting multiple values, integers, floats, or complex field widths; not for a simple two-operand string join.\n\nstd::format would make the code syntactically cleaner but the claim that it is more efficient does not hold for a single-string concatenation. The current implementation is fine as-is.",
      "parentUuid": "5b2de9f8_a54de351",
      "revId": "232f6539393cee755b4c651d1207a9c335847af4",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
