      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T05:41:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked up the behavior of the global `errno` behavior in this scenario:\n\n\"When using C++ std::fstream with exceptions enabled, errno is not guaranteed to be reliable or preserved inside a catch block.By default, std::fstream fails silently. If you intentionally enable exceptions via .exceptions(), the thrown std::ios_base::failure can trigger intermediate cleanup or platform-specific teardown code before your catch block runs. This secondary internal processing can overwrite the global errno value.\"",
      "revId": "232f6539393cee755b4c651d1207a9c335847af4",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a4166e3_6ab1ad06",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/include/utility/vpd_specific_utility.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000353
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T08:49:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To fix it-\nerrno must be saved inside the try block, at the exact point of failure, before any destructor runs. The only reliable way to do that is- disable exceptions and check manually . I will make this change",
      "parentUuid": "9833c363_d852c85c",
      "revId": "232f6539393cee755b4c651d1207a9c335847af4",
